# Visual and first-use audit correction — 2026-11-17

Scope: D-01, D-13 and V-01–20 from the supplied audit. Owner: visual_docs
implementer. Existing uncommitted work was preserved; pre-edit bytes are retained
under `/tmp/ox-audit-visual-before` (local recovery, not portable evidence).
The Visual Studio 2026 Enterprise baseline remains a target, without a native
parity or assistive-technology approval in this correction.

Skills actually read: `.codex/skills/iced-engineering/SKILL.md` (Iced 0.14 widget,
focus and platform boundaries) and `.codex/skills/rust/SKILL.md` (safe API changes
and focused Cargo verification). Manifests: edition 2024, Rust 1.99 floor,
Iced =0.14.0; no dependency or toolchain change.

## Disposition by finding

| Finding | Assessment | Correction / remaining limit |
| --- | --- | --- |
| D-01 | Confirmed | First-use READMEs now enter through Boas-vindas/Abrir pastas…/Tarefas and use actual pt-BR actions; current workbench/recents included. Sequence/first-run text and SVG text updated. Historical screenshots remain identified as 03 November. SVG geometry was preserved and XML parsed; rendering not reobserved. |
| D-13 | Confirmed | Consolidated first-use project-entry and Settings descriptions; removed obsolete manual-menu and Details claims; toolbar shortcut semantics explicit. |
| V-01 | Confirmed | Removed unreachable Settings specimen block, its unused helper and duplicate unreachable match arms. Corrected DESIGN/components/surfaces claims. |
| V-02 | Confirmed | 27 destinations/26 geometries with shared S09/S13 cog stated consistently. |
| V-03 | Confirmed | Removed obsolete 1100/368 geometry claims; source inventory now names 900/1200/1400 and S01 280/210. Header changes from V-18 are documented as 56 workbench/52 welcome logical units (source geometry). |
| V-04 | Confirmed | Fixed-sidebar successor explicitly supersedes old narrow stacking claims; S01 remains side by side at 210 units below 900. |
| V-05 | Confirmed | Current runtime signatures distinguished from retained historical mascot artwork; reference coverage records the successor. |
| V-06 | Partly confirmed | Every tracked native input now shares palette boundary/focus and radius 4, including the five previously unstyled fields. Target-versus-current panel radii documented; generic panel radius 6 versus target editor/chip radii remains a design gap, not silently revised target. |
| V-07 | Confirmed documentary overclaim | DESIGN now limits generation agreement to theme color roles. Scales/type/proposals are metadata and not generated. Current geometry is documented. Extending generation and changing density/navigation design remain separate work. |
| V-08 | Partly confirmed | Removed the claim that every legacy reference value has a native token. Unused role availability alone is not a runtime bug; roles were not deleted. |
| V-09 | Confirmed metadata ambiguity | Proposed direction-B duplicates and metadata-version mismatch remain outside the implemented theme map; consolidation requires a chosen proposal/schema and is left unresolved, not approved. No operational palette change. |
| V-10 | Partly refuted / corrected | Equal focus/selection hue alone does not violate the documented distinct-marker requirement: persistent side marker and focus perimeter differ in geometry. Pressed now has a two-unit border versus hover one-unit. No claim that this establishes native accessibility. |
| V-11 | Confirmed | Focused buttons now use opaque surface_base/text_primary/focus in every role, so the border has contrast against its inside surface even on branded chrome. Added all-role/all-theme style contrast regression and expanded palette background checks; no offset/raster claim. |
| V-12 | Confirmed platform gap | DESIGN/components explicitly state no AccessKit integration in this Iced build and unimplemented AT names/announcements. Settings hover-only label is an explicit user choice, preserved rather than overridden by the audit. Wayland CSD composition remains unobserved. |
| V-13 | Partly confirmed | Analysis clarifies unknown installed build and same-theme comparison limitation. Public source-image hashes remain source identity, not installed Enterprise evidence. Historical temporary path is identified as unavailable reproduction metadata. No fabricated version/build. |
| V-14 | Confirmed omission; coordinator handoff | Fira Sans/Iced Icons bundled by the selected dependency features require provenance inventory outside this writer's assigned font-provenance file. Coordinator notified. |
| V-15 | Confirmed | S01 flow/backend corrected to project entry; S13 title Configurações and NotApplicable badge state documented. Domain workflow states and five evidence verdicts describe different dimensions, so no false one-to-one mapping was added. S13/S14 share settings canvas. |
| V-16 | Partly confirmed | Documented direct session toolbar theme/density shortcuts versus explicit preview/Save/Back in Settings; added Sair inventory. Two access paths alone do not prove competing or broken preference state. |
| V-17 | Confirmed | Synthetic diff uses demonstracao: cor=ambar/azul instead of real oracle result=41/42. Existing demonstration label retained. |
| V-18 | Confirmed | Both signatures now use 128×40 logical units, matching the supplied minimum at scale 1; header dimensions updated. Native resize/scaling/brand legibility remains pending. |
| V-19 | Confirmed | Joined geometry numbers repaired in assigned DESIGN/component/surface prose and internal IDs labelled as control IDs. |
| V-20 | Confirmed authority ambiguity | Header now distinguishes reusable §1–16 requirements, dated observations and current inventory. Old conflicting geometry descriptions corrected in place; no file/anchor migration or broad history rewrite. Structural history extraction is a suggestion, not implemented. |

## Checks actually observed

All commands ran from the Ox root unless the application directory is specified.
No full scanner suite, downloads, commit, publication or graphical session ran.

| Method | Observed result | Limit |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `CARGO_HOME="$PWD/../.cache/ox/cargo-home" cargo test --locked --offline -p ox-ui` in application | exit 0; 48 unit tests passed, 1 subprocess helper ignored at top level (exercised by parent tests); 4 local_task integration + 1 shell contract passed | No native interaction or rendering evidence |
| same Cargo environment, `cargo clippy --locked --offline -p ox-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` | exit 0 after final input/style changes | Static lint/compile only |
| same Cargo environment, `cargo fmt --all -- --check` | exit 0 | Formatting only |
| `python3 application/tools/build_design.py --check` | exit 0; generated roles match controlled source | Themes only, not scales/geometry |
| `python3 application/tools/check_contrast.py` and in-process summary | exit 0; 114/114 role pairs passed; focus pairs minimum 5.006:1 | Opaque palette calculation, not raster or AT conformance |
| Python ElementTree parse of first-run.svg/execution.svg | both parse | SVG text labels changed without geometry regeneration; browser layout unobserved |
| `git diff --check` on assigned paths | exit 0 | Whitespace only |

The configured historical documentation renderer cannot run with its declared
`/tmp/ox-doc-visual-tools` installation: playwright, Mermaid and browser paths are
absent; no `mmdc` executable was found. Its script would also rewrite unrelated
figures and the old 04 November report, so it was not executed. SVG replacements
are bounded text changes with unchanged layout, preserving both diagram structure
and earlier reports; text fit still needs a new renderer observation.

Documentation reviewed/updated: DESIGN, components, surfaces, coverage, Windows
analysis, both READMEs, architecture/application and diagram sources/exports.
Affected feature spec/plan/tasks/evidence disposition belongs to the coordinator:
product-visual-workbench and windows-design-baseline inputs changed. Earlier
native observations cannot approve this revision. In particular PE/SS header and
Settings observations require fresh native checks. No hashes were renewed to
reuse old native evidence.

